==Strategy==
This level's design is simple, to the point where spamming Area Attackers like [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] and meatshields is enough to win.

On higher crown difficulties, you'll have to watch out a little more, as even with the spam of Sir Rels you won't have much cash to work with. Have a dense 75¢ meatshield spam ready to go, stack up Slapsticks, and pack an anti-Relic CC unit like [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Talented Rodeo]] for the Oldhorn.

You can also bring a research [[Cat Combo]] (L) and spam [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] to rush the stage.

==Trivia==
*Despite the name, there are no seahorses (i.e. [[Tackey]] variants) in this stage.

